{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3.11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3.11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int N=1e5+10;\nconst int mod=1e9+7;\ntypedef unsigned long long ull;\n\nint n,m,tt=0,ch[N][64],p[10][10],q[10][64],f[10][N];\nmap<ull,int> id;\n\nint qpow(int a,int b) {\n\tint ret=1;\n\twhile(b) {\n\t\tif(b&1) ret=1ll*ret*a%mod;\n\t\ta=1ll*a*a%mod,b>>=1;\n\t}\n\treturn ret;\n}\n\nint dfs(ull s) {\n\tif(id[s]) return id[s];\n\tid[s]=++tt;\n\tfor(int i=0;i<(1<<n);i++) {\n\t\tull t=s;\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<(1<<n);j++)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<n;k++)\n\t\t\t\tif((j>>k&1)&&(i>>k&1)&&(s>>(j^(1<<k))&1)) t|=1llu<<j;\n\t\tch[id[s]][i]=dfs(t);\n\t}\n\treturn id[s];\n}\n\nint main() {\n\tcin>>n;dfs(1);\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) cin>>p[i][j],p[i][j]=1ll*p[i][j]*qpow(100,mod-2)%mod;\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<(1<<n);j++) {\n\t\t\tq[i][j]=1;\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<n;k++) {\n\t\t\t\tif(j>>k&1) q[i][j]=1ll*q[i][j]*p[k][i]%mod;\n\t\t\t\telse q[i][j]=1ll*q[i][j]*(mod+1-p[k][i])%mod;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\tf[0][1]=1;\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=1;j<=tt;j++)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<(1<<n);k++) f[i+1][ch[j][k]]=(f[i+1][ch[j][k]]+1ll*f[i][j]*q[i][k])%mod;\n\tif(n<6) cout<<f[n][id[(1llu<<(1<<n))-1]];\n\telse cout<<f[n][id[18446744073709551615llu]];\n\treturn 0;\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "openai/gpt-4.1-nano"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nn = int(input())\n\n# Constants\nmod = 10**9 + 7\n\n# Function to perform modular exponentiation\ndef qpow(a, b, mod=mod):\n    ret = 1\n    while b:\n        if b & 1:\n            ret = ret * a % mod\n        a = a * a % mod\n        b >>= 1\n    return ret\n\n# Recursive DFS with memoization\nid_map = {}\ntt = 0\nN = 10**5 + 10\n\n# Since the maximum number of nodes is not explicitly specified, \n# we will simulate with a dictionary\nch = {}\np = [[0]*10 for _ in range(10)]\nq = [[0]*64 for _ in range(10)]\nf = [[0]*N for _ in range(10)]\n\ndef dfs(s):\n    nonlocal tt\n    if s in id_map:\n        return id_map[s]\n    tt += 1\n    id_map[s] = tt\n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        t = s\n        for j in range(1 << n):\n            for k in range(n):\n                if (j >> k & 1) and (i >> k & 1) and ((s >> (j ^ (1 << k))) & 1):\n                    t |= 1 << j\n        ch[(id_map[s], i)] = dfs(t)\n    return id_map[s]\n\nn = int(input())\ndfs(1)\n\n# Read probabilities and convert to modular fractions\nfor i in range(n):\n    row = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    for j in range(n):\n        p[i][j] = row[j] * qpow(100, mod - 2) % mod\n\nfor i in range(n):\n    for j in range(1 << n):\n        q[i][j] = 1\n        for k in range(n):\n            if j >> k & 1:\n                q[i][j] = q[i][j] * p[k][i] % mod\n            else:\n                q[i][j] = q[i][j] * ((mod + 1 - p[k][i]) % mod) % mod\n\n# Initialize f\nf = [[0] * (N) for _ in range(n + 1)]\nf[0][1] = 1\n\n# Main DP loop\nfor i in range(n):\n    for j in range(1, tt + 1):\n        for k in range(1 << n):\n            key = (i, ch.get((j, k), 0))\n            if key in ch:\n                f[i+1][ch[(j, k)]] = (f[i+1][ch[(j, k)]] + f[i][j] * q[i][k]) % mod\n\n# Final output\nfull_mask = (1 << (1 << n)) - 1\nif n < 6:\n    result = f[n][id_map.get(full_mask, 0)]\nelse:\n    result = f[n][id_map.get((1 << 64) - 1, 0)]\n\nprint(result)\n\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.9\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0005081149865873158, -7.64839569455944e-05, -4.320199877838604e-07, -2.7729658540920354e-05, -0.009675342589616776, -0.5232686400413513, 0.0, 0.0, -0.9178466796875, -0.8792503476142883, -1.6751856803894043, -0.024926045909523964, -0.6100146770477295, -0.00030078491545282304, -0.0008064138819463551, -0.0004261468129698187, -0.00861456897109747, -9.088346359931165e-07, -0.002185118617489934, -0.0009171743295155466, -1.9361264946837764e-07, -0.0559372678399086, -0.3491322696208954, -0.9907585978507996, -2.127397298812866, -0.7628092169761658, -0.09204868227243423, -0.04345299303531647, -3.128163257315464e-07, -0.0021007757168263197, -1.9361264946837764e-07, -0.00016241880075540394, -6.372916686814278e-05, -8.017927029868588e-05, -0.004685614723712206, -1.1472419600977446e-06, -6.876039981842041, -0.260240375995636, -0.6326970458030701, -0.0022447004448622465, -2.816093228830141e-06, -3.7697225252486533e-06, -0.0012951197568327188, -0.003177952254191041, -1.1517960956552997e-05, -3.128163257315464e-07, -4.320199877838604e-07, -9.088346359931165e-07, -0.049402713775634766, 0.0, -0.007613136898726225, -1.9361264946837764e-07, 0.0, -4.668304245569743e-05, -4.320199877838604e-07, -4.246537173457909e-06, -1.9361264946837764e-07, -2.165027217415627e-05, -1.8624639324116288e-06, -5.512236498361744e-07, -6.704273118884885e-07, -1.31326425075531, -1.9361264946837764e-07, -5.512236498361744e-07, 0.0, -1.8624639324116288e-06, -5.512236498361744e-07, -1.9361264946837764e-07, -1.0280383548888494e-06, -1.3856492842023727e-06, -0.0004890497075393796, 0.0, -1.8624639324116288e-06, 0.0, -5.9153885558771435e-06, -1.7432603272027336e-06, -4.320199877838604e-0